NAME
    runto - resume emulation until a named event or address

SYNOPSIS
    runto nmi | irq | brk | cop
    runto scanline <n>
    runto frame [<n>]
    runto <addr>

DESCRIPTION
    Arms a target event and resumes emulation, halting at the next
    instruction boundary once the event occurs. An armed event survives
    plain resume(1) until it fires; arming a second run-to of the same
    kind replaces the first.

OPTIONS
    nmi | irq | brk | cop
        Resume until the main CPU takes an interrupt of the named kind,
        halting inside the handler.

    scanline <n>
        Resume until decimal scanline <n> starts in the current or next
        frame.

    frame [<n>]
        Resume until decimal frame <n> completes (defaults to the next
        frame when <n> is omitted).

    <addr>
        Add a regular breakpoint at hex address <addr> (or label name) and
        resume. Prints the created breakpoint ID; the breakpoint remains
        active after firing until removed with 'bp remove <id>'.

EXAMPLES
    runto nmi
    runto scanline 100
    runto frame
    runto 808000

EXIT STATUS
    0   Run-to armed and resume requested (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    step(1), bp(1), bt(1), resume(1), vectors(1), label(1)
